      "text": "53-year-old male presenting with joint pain and morning stiffness for 2 months. Character: pain in small joints of both hands; radiation: n/a; aggravated by cold weather; relieved by warm water bath. Severity 7/10. Associated: low grade fever, tiredness, swelling of joints. PMH: Hypertension for 2 years. Drugs: Amlodipine 5 mg. Allergy: no known allergies. Family: no similar illness. Personal: chews tobacco. Triage: ROUTINE."
